From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CEB-GNRD board layer <bmc@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] post codes: newest first

The POST Code table is meant to be sorted by "id", descending, but the items
have no "id", so the codes were listed in the order the service returns them,
oldest first.  Give each code its position in that order.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD board-specific]
---
--- a/src/store/modules/Logs/PostCodeLogsStore.js
+++ b/src/store/modules/Logs/PostCodeLogsStore.js
@@ -20,9 +20,13 @@ const PostCodeLogsStore = {
           `${await this.dispatch('global/getSystemPath')}/LogServices/PostCodes/Entries`,
         )
         .then(({ data: { Members = [] } = {} }) => {
-          const postCodeLogs = Members.map((log) => {
+          // The service lists the codes oldest first.  The table sorts by "id"
+          // (descending, newest first), but the items had no such field, so the
+          // list was shown oldest first: number the codes in service order.
+          const postCodeLogs = Members.map((log, index) => {
             const { Created, MessageArgs, AdditionalDataURI } = log;
             return {
+              id: index,
               date: new Date(Created),
               bootCount: MessageArgs[0],
               timeStampOffset: MessageArgs[1],
